0..75 Comment "// Handlers of an `extern` block\'s interface written in gandr, each refused"
76..115 Comment "// where it leaves the block\'s members."
116..118 Comment "//"
119..194 Comment "// A clause answers a member that the block declares. It binds the member\'s"
195..273 Comment "// arguments as one payload, or none for a member of no argument, and then the"
274..344 Comment "// resumption. Each argument keeps its fixed-width type in the clause."
345..347 Comment "//"
348..421 Comment "// The first handler answers `sub`, which the block does not declare. The"
422..498 Comment "// second binds only the resumption of `add`, which takes two arguments. The"
499..550 Comment "// third sums the two `u32` arguments as `Integer`."
551..553 Comment "//"
554..632 Comment "// - see: `model/interop/boundary/round-trip.gandr` — a handler that answers"
633..656 Comment "//   the block in gandr"
658..732 Comment "// The boundary check reads `admitBlock` here, whatever the listing names."
